[gd_scene load_steps=9 format=3]

; BASE-1 (2026-09-19) — THE SEARCH ROOM. 14 x 10 x 3.5 m interior box, same construction as
; HoldingRoom.tscn (read that file's header for the convention and for why nothing here may be
; built in code). Wider than the other two on its long axis because SHELF-1 fills it with aisles
; and the hider needs somewhere to walk between them.
;
; EMPTY ON PURPOSE. BASE-1 authors the shell and nothing else: the shelves, the bins, the rack of
; near-miss objects and the drop-off bin are SHELF-1's and BTN-1's, and an empty box is a cheaper
; thing for them to fill than a box full of guesses.

